          <!-- Sports Resources -->
          <div class="resources mb-5">
            <h3 class="mb-4">Sports Resources</h3>
            <p>
              Sports are organized physical activities that encourage the
              display of skill by the competing parties. They foster lifelong
              habits of health and well-being.
            </p>

            <h5 class="mt-4">Key Elements of Sports</h5>
            <ul>
              <li>Involves physical movement, techniques, or exertion.</li>
              <li>Guided by rules and standards for fair play.</li>
              <li>Requires skills developed through training and strategy.</li>
              <li>Centered on competition and performance.</li>
              <li>Can be both recreational and professional.</li>
            </ul>

            <h5 class="mt-4">Types of Sports</h5>
            <ul>
              <li>
                <strong>Team Sports:</strong> Football, basketball, volleyball.
              </li>
              <li>
                <strong>Individual Sports:</strong> Tennis, golf, swimming.
              </li>
              <li><strong>Combat Sports:</strong> Boxing, judo, wrestling.</li>
              <li>
                <strong>Racket Sports:</strong> Tennis, badminton, squash.
              </li>
            </ul>

            <h5 class="mt-4">Purposes and Benefits of Sports</h5>
            <ul>
              <li>
                <strong>Physical Fitness:</strong> Improves cardiovascular
                health and strength.
